11. Audit Log and Cryptographic Integrity

The audit log is a safety-critical component, not an afterthought.

Each log entry is:

L_t =
\left(
\hat{x}_t,
\mathbf{U}_t,
\bar{\mathbf{T}}_t,
a_t^{\text{requested}},
a_t^{\text{final}},
m_t,
\Phi_t,
E_t,
M_t,
\Delta t_{\text{latch}},
v_t^{\text{human}},
h_{t-1}
\right),

where v_t^{\text{human}} is the human verification or override statement, and h_{t-1} is the previous hash.

Hash chain:

h_t = H\left( L_t \parallel h_{t-1} \right),
\quad
h_0 = \text{genesis}.

Each entry is signed with Ed25519. Periodic Merkle roots are anchored to write-once read-many (WORM) storage.

This design follows deployed body-camera and evidence-integrity systems.

