Appendix H — Proxy-Bias Detection Details

H.1 Conditional Mutual Information

The conditional mutual information between operational features \hat{x}^{op} and protected identity g is:

I(\hat{x}^{op}; g \mid y)
=
\sum_{g, \hat{x}^{op}, y}
p(g, \hat{x}^{op}, y)
\log
\frac{
p(\hat{x}^{op}, g \mid y)
}{
p(\hat{x}^{op} \mid y)
p(g \mid y)
}.

In practice, finite-sample estimators such as k-nearest-neighbor mutual information or binning are used. This is an intended future implementation, not an evaluated component of this manuscript.

H.2 Adversarial Bias Classifier

An adversarial classifier f_{\text{bias}} is trained to predict g from \hat{x}^{op}. Balanced accuracy:

B_{\text{acc}} =
\frac{1}{|\mathcal{G}|}
\sum_{g \in \mathcal{G}}
\text{recall}_g.

If:

B_{\text{acc}} > \delta_{\text{acc}},

a bias alert is raised.

H.3 Fairness Metrics

Equalized odds difference:

\Delta_{\text{EO}} =
\max_{y \in \{0,1\}}
\left|
P(\hat{Y}=1 \mid Y=y, G=g_1)
-
P(\hat{Y}=1 \mid Y=y, G=g_2)
\right|.

Disparate impact ratio:

\mathrm{DIR} =
\frac{
P(F > F_0 \mid G=g_1)
}{
P(F > F_0 \mid G=g_2)
}.

The framework sets provisional thresholds:

\Delta_{\text{EO}} \le 0.05,

0.8 \le \mathrm{DIR} \le 1.25.

These are governance parameters, not universal constants.

H.4 Feedback-Loop Detection

The monitor estimates:

\Delta_g(t)
=
P(\text{high risk} \mid g, t)
-
P(\text{high risk} \mid g, t-1).

If the change in group-specific risk cannot be explained by underlying incident data, the system flags a potential feedback loop.

